<deviceset name="WE-RCDS_791002002" urn="urn:adsk.eagle:component:53248493/1" prefix="IC">
<description>WE-RCDS Residual Current Detection Sensor

for fault current detection in EV-charging applications 

Characteristics 
Compact design for PCB board mounting 
DC 6mA residual direct current detecting RDC-M-Module for mode 3 EV charging 
System fault indication 
Supply voltage drop monitoring 
Module Software certified according to ANSI/UL 1998, Class 1 
Relevant EMC tests according to IEC 62955: 2018 and EN 60730-1 

Applications 
DC- Residual current detection sensor for stationary EV charging devices
To meet IEC 61851-1 (ensure the disconnection of the supply in case of DC fault)
If the Residual Current Detection Sensor WE-RCDS is to be used in combination with a residual current device RCD type A, this offer is directed exclusively at customers who are authorized to use the patent EP 2 571 128 B3 (valid in Austria, Switzerland/Liechtenstein, Germany, Spain, France, Great Britain and Norway) and the parallel property rights CN 103 001 175 B, US 9,397,494 B2 and DE 10 2011 082 941 A1 or who do not offer, manufacture and distribute within the scope of these property rights.

Details see:  www.we-online.com/en/components/products/WE-RCDS

Created by Ella 2024-03-18
2024 (C) Würth Elektronik</description>
